% You are an expert Python engineer. Implement pdd/story_criteria.py.

<pdd-dependency>detect_change_python.prompt</pdd-dependency>

% Purpose
Gate `pdd detect --stories` on a bounded, per-acceptance-criterion judgement instead
of on whether an open-ended detector volunteered zero suggestions. The legacy pass
criterion ("the model proposed no changes") measures model strength rather than the
prompts: a weaker model fails a correct prompt set, and the same inputs flip verdict
on `--strength` alone.

% Contract
- Parse the `## Acceptance Criteria` section of a story contract or story into
  ordered `AcceptanceCriterion` records identified `AC1`..`ACn`. Numbered and
  bulleted list items are both accepted; continuation lines fold into the item
  above them; parsing MUST stop at the next heading.
- Absence of a criteria section, or a section with no list items, MUST return an
  empty list so the caller can fall back to the legacy detector.
- Classify every criterion exactly once as `satisfied`, `unsatisfied`, or
  `unclear`. Only `unsatisfied` fails a story.
- `unclear` MUST be advisory and MUST NOT affect the verdict; a hedging model must
  not be able to fail a correct prompt set.
- A criterion the evaluator returned no assessment for MUST be `unevaluated`, and
  MUST make the evaluation incomplete rather than passing. Silence is never
  approval.
- A `satisfied` status MUST carry a verbatim citation from the evaluated prompts;
  without one it degrades to `unclear`. Report whether the citation was found
  verbatim, but MUST NOT fail a criterion for an unverifiable citation, since
  models paraphrase and a false alarm would restore model sensitivity.
- An unrecognized or empty status MUST become `unclear`, never `satisfied`.
- Criterion identifiers MUST be matched loosely (`AC1`, `ac-1`, `1`, `criterion 1`);
  unknown identifiers are dropped and duplicates keep the first assessment.
- A malformed evaluator response or missing template MUST raise
  `StoryCriteriaError` carrying the cost already incurred, never return an empty
  (passing) verdict set.
- Untrusted model text MUST be collapsed to one bounded single-line string before
  it reaches logs, JSON, or terminal output.

% Capabilities
- Render `unsatisfied` verdicts as `detect_change`-shaped
  `{prompt_name, change_instructions}` rows so `pdd fix`, story-link caching, and
  the evidence document keep working unchanged.
- Summarize an evaluation as per-status counts.

% Non-responsibilities
- MUST NOT mutate prompts, stories, or contracts.
- MUST NOT decide story-level PASS/FAIL reporting, render terminal output, or write
  result documents; those belong to `user_story_tests` and `story_detection_result`.
- MUST NOT modify or replace `detect_change`, which remains the propagation
  detector and the legacy fallback gate.

% Interface
- `parse_acceptance_criteria(contract_text) -> list[AcceptanceCriterion]`
- `evaluate_acceptance_criteria(prompt_files, story_content, criteria, strength,
  temperature, time, verbose) -> CriteriaEvaluation`
- `changes_from_verdicts(verdicts, default_prompt_name) -> list[dict[str, str]]`
- `evaluation_summary(evaluation) -> tuple[int, int, int, int]`
- `CriteriaEvaluation` exposes `verdicts`, `cost`, `model`, and the derived
  `unsatisfied`, `unclear`, `unevaluated`, `passed`, and `complete` properties.

% Implementation notes
- Send the bounded classification through `llm_invoke` with a structured output
  model in a single call; the template is `story_criteria_LLM`.
- Preprocess the template with `double_curly_brackets=True`, excluding
  `PROMPT_LIST`, `STORY_CONTENT`, and `CRITERIA_LIST`.
